{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a752879911a4b44e9","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a883ed86f0a5df7d","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace/649c3b71-f1fd-46a9-a844-34ab62b5da5e/tasks/a752879911a4b44e9.output","summary":"All three prompt files are in the inbox with correct frontmatter. Here is my report.\n\n## Files created (execution order)\n\n- `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-002-config-job-namespace-model.md` — `JobNamespace` field on `ConfigSpec` (+ `Equal`), `ResolveJobNamespace` function, `AgentConfiguration` field + `TaggedConfigurations` copy, resolver `convert` propagation, CRD schema registration, and boundary tests. Covers ACs 2, 3, 4.\n- `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-002-config-job-namespace-spawner.md` — spawner wiring: resolved-namespace Create target, refuse-on-error with ERROR log, unconditional `app: agent` pod-template label, the three stdlib AC tests, mechanical updates to existing Ginkgo spawner tests, CHANGELOG entry. Covers ACs 5, 6, 7.\n- `/workspace/prompts/3-spec-002-config-job-namespace-doc.md` — CRD doc Fields-table row with the default and rejection rule. Covers AC 8.\n\nExecution order is the numbered prefix (1 → 2 → 3); prompt 3 is docs-only and depends on nothing but settled semantics. This matches the spec's own 3-prompt decomposition (which I kept — it is correctly sized).\n\n## Key decisions\n\n- **`ResolveJobNamespace` is a package-level function in `k8s/apis/.../v1`, not a `Validate` hook.** The rejection is a runtime per-executor guard (the same CRD is shared across dev/prod executors), so it must not be an admission check. Signature `func ResolveJobNamespace(ctx context.Context, jobNamespace string, executorNamespace string) (string, error)`, error message carries the exact AC substring `may not equal the executor namespace`.\n- **Prompt 1 also registers the field in `pkg/k8s_connector.go` `configSpecProperties()`.** The spec's decomposition didn't list this, but the loud comment above `configSpecSchema` documents the v0.5.0 `maxConcurrentJobs` incident: an unregistered field is silently pruned by the API server on every executor restart. Without this step the field would be inert in prod. It ships with a level-1 boundary test in a new internal test file.\n- **Prompt 2 requires updating ~25 existing Ginkgo spawner tests.** The default `<executor>-agents-sandbox` moves where created jobs land, so every `Jobs(\"test-ns\")` List/Get verification and the AlreadyExists pre-seeded fixture move to `test-ns-agents-sandbox`. A blanket replace of the `Jobs(\"test-ns\")` literal in the test file is safe (the IsJobActive fixtures use `fake.NewClientset(job)`, a different pattern). This is the biggest ripple in the spec and is called out explicitly.\n- **The `app: agent` label is implemented as a post-build `applyAppLabel(job)` guard** (mirroring `applyTaskIDLabel`/`applyAssigneeLabel`), keeping the existing `jobBuilder.SetApp(\"agent\")`. This makes the \"conflicting label overwritten\" part of AC 6 testable directly in a new internal `package spawner` test file.\n- **AC tests are plain stdlib `Test*` functions** (`TestResolveJobNamespace`, `TestSpawnTargetNamespace`, `TestSpawnRejectsExecutorNamespace`, `TestJobPodLabels`), because the AC verification `go test ./... -run ... -v` requires `--- PASS: TestXxx` output that Ginkgo `It` specs cannot produce. This deliberately overrides the repo's Ginkgo convention for these specific tests only; all other new tests stay Ginkgo.\n- **CHANGELOG** entry (one `feat:` bullet covering the whole feature) appended to the existing `## Unreleased` in prompt 2.\n\n## Open questions left as comments in the prompts\n\n1. **IsJobActive / CountActiveJobs / JobWatcher namespace gap (the significant one).** This spec only moves the *create* path into the sandbox. `IsJobActive` and `CountActiveJobs` (executor-ns `List`) and the `JobWatcher` informer (`WithNamespace`) still observe only the executor namespace, so sandboxed Jobs would be invisible to the duplicate-spawn guard, the concurrency cap, and zombie/failure handling. The spec's ACs and DBs do not address this, and the spec Non-goal only covers *Config* watching. I did NOT change those paths (that would be scope invention); I flagged it as an OPEN QUESTION in prompt 2's constraints and adapted the existing \"SpawnJob + IsJobActive label contract\" test to preserve its label-key regression intent. The reviewer should decide whether a follow-up spec re-scopes these lookups.\n2. **\"Conflicting `app` label overwritten\" interpretation.** Since the spawner builds its own job with no injection point for a conflicting label, AC 6's second half is implemented as a direct unit test of `applyAppLabel` on a hand-built job with a pre-seeded conflicting `app` value. A reviewer may want to confirm that matches the AC's intent.\n3. **stdlib-vs-Ginkgo tension** for the four AC tests — required by the ACs' `-run`/`-v` output expectations; noted in prompts 1 and 2 so the auditor doesn't flag it as a convention violation.\n\n## Docs referenced in `<context>`\n\n- Project: `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md`; repo files `k8s/apis/.../types.go`, `types_test.go`, `zz_generated.deepcopy.go`, `pkg/agent_configuration.go`, `pkg/config_resolver.go`, `pkg/k8s_connector.go`, `pkg/spawner/job_spawner.go`, `pkg/spawner/job_spawner_test.go`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/agent-crd-specification.md`.\n- Coding plugin (in-container paths): `go-patterns.md`, `go-error-wrapping-guide.md`, `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-glog-guide.md`, `go-kubernetes-crd-controller-guide.md`, `changelog-guide.md`, `definition-of-done.md`, `documentation-guide.md`.\n\n## Inlined patterns (no doc exists for them)\n\nThe `applyAppLabel` nil-map-guard pattern follows the existing in-file `applyTaskIDLabel`/`applyAssigneeLabel` precedent, so no new project doc is needed. The CRD-schema-pruning rule is already documented in `k8s_connector.go`'s own comment, which the prompt cites rather than re-inventing.\n\n## Sug