{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94e6fe00e21214ec","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"002-config-job-namespace\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-03T17:50:40Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t<summary>\n8\t- Config authors can set a `jobNamespace` on a Config to place that agent's Jobs in a namespace other than the executor's.\n9\t- Leaving `jobNamespace` unset resolves to a per-environment sandbox namespace — an executor in `dev` resolves `dev-agents-sandbox`, an executor in `prod` resolves `prod-agents-sandbox` — so dev and prod never share a sandbox.\n10\t- Setting `jobNamespace` to the executor's own namespace is rejected with an explicit error whose message names the rule, so no Config can opt out of isolation.\n11\t- Existing Config CRs stay valid unedited — the new field is additive and optional.\n12\t- The resolved namespace value flows end-to-end from the Config CR through the resolver into the runtime configuration object the spawner consumes.\n13\t- The new field is registered in the executor's CRD schema so the API server does not prune it (the executor re-applies this schema on every start).\n14\t- The resolution rule is pinned by a table-driven test covering the exact cases the spec names: dev+empty, prod+empty, an explicit other-namespace, and the reject case.\n15\t</summary>\n16\t\n17\t<objective>\n18\tAdd the optional `jobNamespace` field to the Config CRD and a `ResolveJobNamespace` derivation/rejection function so the executor can later spawn Jobs outside its own namespace, defaulting to the safe per-environment sandbox and refusing any attempt to use the executor's own namespace. This prompt makes the field exist and resolve correctly end-to-end; the spawner wiring that consumes the resolved value ships in the next prompt.\n19\t</objective>\n20\t\n21\t<context>\n22\tRead `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` for project conventions (Ginkgo/Gomega v2, `github.com/bborbe/errors` wrapping, glog V(n) gating, coverage ≥80% for new code).\n23\t\n24\tRead these files fully before changing anything:\n25\t- `/workspace/k8s/apis/agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1/types.go` — `ConfigSpec` struct (the `Equal` method and `Validate` method at the bottom), the existing field-declaration style (doc comment + json tag, e.g. `PriorityClassName string \\`json:\"priorityClassName,omitempty\"\\``), the `errors` import already present.\n26\t- `/workspace/k8s/apis/agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1/types_test.go` — mirror the existing per-field `Describe` blocks exactly: \"JSON round-trip for priorityClassName\" (~line 225) and \"Equal with priorityClassName\" (~line 252). The file is `package v1_test` with a Ginkgo suite entry `TestV1`.\n27\t- `/workspace/k8s/apis/agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1/zz_generated.deepcopy.go` — confirm `ConfigSpec.DeepCopyInto` does `*out = *in` first; a new `string` field needs NO generator run.\n28\t- `/workspace/pkg/agent_configuration.go` — `AgentConfiguration` struct (note: it carries `PriorityClassName`, `Trigger`, `ZombieJobTimeoutSeconds` — fields mirrored from `ConfigSpec`) and `TaggedConfigurations` which copies every field explicitly.\n29\t- `/workspace/pkg/config_resolver.go` — the `convert` function (copies `ConfigSpec` fields into `AgentConfiguration`).\n30\t- `/workspace/pkg/k8s_connector.go` — the `configSpecSchema` / `configSpecProperties` region (the doc comment above `configSpecSchema` explains why every field MUST be registered here or the API server prunes it; see the v0.5.0 `maxConcurrentJobs` incident note).\n31\t- `/workspace/pkg/config_resolver_test.go` — the first `It(\"returns converted AgentConfiguration with image tag appended\", ...)` which asserts each converted field.\n32\t- `/workspace/pkg/agent_configuration_test.go` — the `Describe(\"TaggedConfigurations\", ...)` block's field-preservation specs.\n33\t\n34\tRelevant docs (in-container paths):\n35\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-patterns.md` — public API + private struct conventions, error wrapping.\n36\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md` — never `fmt.Errorf`; `errors.Errorf(ctx, ...)` for a new error without a cause.\n37\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega, coverage ≥80% for new code, external vs internal test packages.\n38\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-kubernetes-crd-controller-guide.md` — CRD field registration patterns.\n39\t</context>\n40\t\n41\t<requirements>\n42\tThe end state: the Config CRD carries an optional `jobNamespace`, a `ResolveJobNamespace` function implements the spec's resolution rule (empty → `<executorNamespace>-agents-sandbox`, explicit value → that value, executor's own namespace → error), the value flows through the resolver into `AgentConfiguration`, and the executor's CRD schema registers the field so the API server keeps it.\n43\t\n44\t1. Add the `JobNamespace` field to `ConfigSpec` in `/workspace/k8s/apis/agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1/types.go`. Insert it after `PriorityClassName` (both are Job-stamping fields) with the same style as the neighbouring fields:\n45\t   ```go\n46\t   // JobNamespace is the Kubernetes namespace the agent's Jobs are spawned into.\n47\t   // Optional; when empty, the executor resolves a per-environment sandbox\n48\t   // namespace (\"<executorNamespace>-agents-sandbox\") so dev and prod never\n49\t   // share a sandbox. Setting it to the executor's own namespace is rejected at\n50\t   // spawn time — no Config can opt out of isolation.\n51\t   JobNamespace string `json:\"jobNamespace,omitempty\"`\n52\t   ```\n53\t\n54\t2. Add `s.JobNamespace == o.JobNamespace` to `ConfigSpec.Equal` in the same file, directly after the `s.PriorityClassName == o.PriorityClassName` line.\n55\t\n56\t3. Add the resolution function to the same file, after the last helper `validateTaskTypesList` (package-level, since it needs the executor namespace which `Validate` does not know — the rejection is a runtime, per-executor guard, NOT an admission check; do NOT call it from `Validate`):\n57\t   ```go\n58\t   // ResolveJobNamespace returns the namespace an agent's Jobs must be spawned\n59\t   // into. An empty jobNamespace resolves to \"<executorNamespace>-agents-sandbox\"\n60\t   // (derived per environment so dev and prod never share a sandbox); any other\n61\t   // value is returned unchanged; a jobNamespace equal to the executor's own\n62\t   // namespace is rejected so no Config can opt out of isolation.\n63\t   func ResolveJobNamespace(ctx context.Context, jobNamespace string, executorNamespace string) (string, error) {\n64\t       if jobNamespace == \"\" {\n65\t           return executorNamespace + \"-agents-sandbox\", nil\n66\t       }\n67\t       if jobNamespace == executorNamespace {\n68\t           return \"\", errors.Errorf(\n69\t               ctx,\n70\t               \"jobNamespace %q may not equal the executor namespace %q\",\n71\t               jobNamespace,\n72\t               executorNamespace,\n73\t           )\n74\t       }\n75\t       return jobNamespace, nil\n76\t   }\n77\t   ```\n78\t   The message MUST contain the exact substring `may not equal the executor namespace` — the spec's acceptance test asserts on it. `errors` is already imported in this file.\n79\t\n80\t4. Create `/workspace/k8s/apis/agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1/job_namespace_test.go` in `package v1_test` (a plain stdlib test file — the spec's acceptance criterion requires `--- PASS: TestResolveJobNamespace` output, which a Ginkgo `It` would not produce; the existing Ginkgo suite in `types_test.go` is untouched). Table-driven test with exactly these cases:\n81\t   ```go\n82\t   func TestResolveJobNamespace(t *testing.T) {\n83\t       tests := []struct {\n84\t           name              string\n85\t           jobNamespace      string\n86\t           executorNamespace string\n87\t           want              string\n88\t           wantErrSubstring  string\n89\t       }{\n90\t           {\"empty resolves to dev-agents-sandbox\", \"\", \"dev\", \"dev-agents-sandbox\", \"\"},\n91\t           {\"empty resolves to prod-agents-sandbox\", \"\", \"prod\", \"prod-agents-sandbox\", \"\"},\n92\t           {\"explicit other-ns is returned unchanged\", \"other-ns\", \"dev\", \"other-ns\", \"\"},\n93\t           {\"executor namespace is rejected\", \"dev\", \"dev\", \"\", \"may not equal the executor namespace\"},\n94\t       }\n95\t       for _, tt := range tests {\n96\t           t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n97\t               got, err := agentv1.ResolveJobNamespace(context.Background(), tt.jobNamespace, tt.executorNamespace)\n98\t               if tt.wantErrSubstring != \"\" {\n99\t                   if err == nil {\n100\t                       t.Fatalf(\"expected error containing %q, got nil\", tt.wantErrSubstring)\n101\t                   }\n102\t                   if !strings.Contains(err.Error(), tt.wantErrSubstring) {\n103\t                       t.Fatalf(\"error %q does not contain %q\", err.Error(), tt.wantErrSubstring)\n104\t                   }\n105\t                   return\n106\t               }\n107\t               if err != nil {\n108\t                   t.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n109\t               }\n110\t               if got != tt.want {\n111\t                   t.Fatalf(\"ResolveJobNamespace(%q, %q) = %q, want %q\", tt.jobNamespace, tt.executorNamespace, got, tt.want)\n112\t               }\n113\t           })\n114\t       }\n115\t   }\n116\t   ```\n117\t   Imports: `context`, `strings`, `testing`, and `agentv1 \"github.com/bborbe/agent-task-executor/k8s/apis/agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1\"`.\n118\t\n119\t5. Add two Ginkgo `Describe` blocks to `/workspace/k8s/apis/agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1/types_test.go`, mirroring the `priorityClassName` pattern verbatim:\n120\t   - `Describe(\"JSON round-trip for jobNamespace\")` with two `It`s: (a) a `ConfigSpec` with `JobNamespace: \"other-ns\"` round-trips — marshal, unmarshal, `Expect(decoded.JobNamespace).To(Equal(\"other-ns\"))`; (b) a `ConfigSpec` without `JobNamespace` marshals WITHOUT the key — `Expect(string(data)).NotTo(ContainSubstring(\"jobNamespace\"))` (this pins the `omitempty` / additive constraint).\n121\t   - `Describe(\"Equal with jobNamespace\")` with two `It`s: (a) returns false when only `JobNamespace` differs; (b) returns true when `JobNamespace` matches.\n122\t\n123\t6. Add the field to the runtime config type in `/workspace/pkg/agent_configuration.go`:\n124\t   - Add to the `AgentConfiguration` struct, after `PriorityClassName`, with a doc comment matching the neighbouring fields:\n125\t     ```go\n126\t     // JobNamespace is the Kubernetes namespace the agent's Jobs are spawned\n127\t     // into. Empty means the executor derives a per-environment sandbox\n128\t     // namespace (\"<executorNamespace>-agents-sandbox\") at spawn time.\n129\t     JobNamespace string\n130\t     ```\n131\t   - Add `JobNamespace: c.JobNamespace,` to the struct literal inside `TaggedConfigurations` (every field is copied explicitly there — do not forget this or the tagged copy drops the value).\n132\t\n133\t7. Propagate the field through the resolver in `/workspace/pkg/config_resolver.go`: in the `AgentConfiguration{...}` literal inside `convert`, add `JobNamespace: obj.Spec.JobNamespace,` (next to `PriorityClassName: obj.Spec.PriorityClassName,`).\n134\t\n135\t8. Register the field in the executor's CRD schema in `/workspace/pkg/k8s_connector.go`: inside `configSpecProperties()`, add `\"jobNamespace\": {Type: \"string\"},` next to the `\"secretName\"` / `\"volumeClaim\"` entries. The doc comment above `configSpecSchema` is authoritative: an unregistered field is silently pruned by the API server from every Config within seconds of the next executor start — this step is what makes the field real in production.\n136\t\n137\t9. Create `/workspace/pkg/k8s_connector_internal_test.go` in `package pkg` (internal test file — the schema funcs are unexported; this mirrors the `pkg/job_watcher_internal_test.go` precedent of an internal test file). This is the boundary test that guards against the silent-prune regression:\n138\t   ```go\n139\t   func TestConfigSpecSchemaIncludesJobNamespace(t *testing.T) {\n140\t       props := configSpecProperties()\n141\t       p, ok := props[\"jobNamespace\"]\n142\t       if !ok {\n143\t           t.Fatal(\"configSpecProperties() missing jobNamespace — the API server will prune the field from every Config on next restart\")\n144\t       }\n145\t       if p.Type != \"string\" {\n146\t           t.Fatalf(\"jobNamespace schema type = %q, want string\", p.Type)\n147\t       }\n148\t   }\n149\t   ```\n150\t\n151\t10. Extend `/workspace/pkg/config_resolver_test.go`: in the first `It(\"returns converted AgentConfiguration with image tag appended\", ...)`, add `JobNamespace: \"sandbox-ns\"` to the `ConfigSpec` literal and assert `Expect(config.JobNamespace).To(Equal(\"sandbox-ns\"))` next to the other converted-field assertions. This is the boundary test proving the field crosses the resolver (Config CR → `AgentConfiguration`).\n152\t\n153\t11. Extend `/workspace/pkg/agent_configuration_test.go`: inside `Describe(\"TaggedConfigurations\", ...)`, add `It(\"preserves JobNamespace\", ...)` that tags `configs` and asserts `tagged[0].JobNamespace` equals the source value (add `JobNamespace: \"sandbox-ns\"` to the package-level `configs` fixture used by those specs if it is not already set there).\n154\t\n155\t12. Do NOT run any code generator. `ConfigSpec.DeepCopyInto` copies the struct first (`*out = *in`), which already covers a plain `string` field — `zz_generated.deepcopy.go` needs no change. Do NOT add `JobNamespace` to `ConfigSpec.Validate` — the executor-namespace rejection is a runtime per-executor guard, not a CRD admission rule (the same CRD is shared across dev/prod executors).\n156\t</requirements>\n157\t\n158\t<constraints>\n159\t- Existing `Config` CRs must remain valid unedited — `JobNamespace` is additive and optional (the JSON `omitempty` test in requirement 5 pins this).\n160\t- The default must be the safe value: omitting the field may never place a Job in the executor's namespace (the reject case in requirement 4 pins this).\n161\t- No new capability, securityContext change, or RBAC grant is introduced by this spec.\n162\t- `TaskType`/`TaskTypes` routing behavior is untouched.\n163\t- Do NOT call `ResolveJobNamespace` from `ConfigSpec.Validate` or `ConfigSpec.Config.Validate` — the executor namespace is a per-executor runtime value unknown at admission time.\n164\t- Do NOT change the `JobSpawner` interface, the `NewJobSpawner` constructor, `pkg/factory/factory.go`, `main.go`, or any signature — the spawner wiring is the next prompt.\n165\t- This prompt does NOT touch `/workspace/pkg/spawner/job_spawner.go` — that is the next prompt.\n166\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n167\t- Existing tests must still pass.\n168\t</constraints>\n169\t\n170\t<verification>\n171\tRun `make test` iteratively after each meaningful change (fast feedback loop), then `make precommit` ONCE at the very end.\n172\t\n173\t- `make test` — exits 0.\n174\t- `make precommit` — exits 0.\n175\t- `go test ./... -run TestResolveJobNamespace -v` — stdout contains `--- PASS: TestResolveJobNamespace` (and each `=== RUN`/`--- PASS` subtest line).\n176\t- `go test -mod=mod -coverprofile=/tmp/cover.out ./k8s/apis/agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1/... ./pkg/... && go tool cover -func=/tmp/cover.out` — `ResolveJobNamespace` is fully covered (the table test hits empty / passthrough / reject branches), and the new `convert` / `TaggedConfigurations` / schema assertions each execute at least once (≥80% statement coverage for new code).\n177\t\n178\tDo NOT run `docker`, `make build`, `kubectl`, `dark-factory`, or `git` commands in this prompt — the container cannot execute them and the daemon does not check their exit codes.\n179\t</verification>\n180\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92879bdf48abd110","session_id":"649c3b71-f1fd-46a9-a844-34ab62b5da5e","uuid":"02c64afc-fbf9-41f7-9108-df08496e5405","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:53:02.389Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1 (model)"}
