{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab0a2e18a41e51f1","type":"tool_result","content":"4:Never use `fmt.Errorf` or bare `return err`. The library enriches errors\n26:| `Errorf` | Create new error with formatted message | `Errorf(ctx, format, args...) error` |\n45:return errors.Errorf(ctx, \"unsupported period type: %s\", periodType)\n100:2. **Never `fmt.Errorf`** — use `errors.Wrapf` (wrapping) or `errors.Errorf` (new error)\n104:6. **Remove unused imports** — after replacing `fmt.Errorf`, remove `\"fmt\"` if unused\n126:    return errors.Errorf(context.Background(), \"invalid: %s\", input)\n131:    return errors.Errorf(ctx, \"invalid: %s\", input)\n135:### Fix: Replace fmt.Errorf\n139:return fmt.Errorf(\"fetch failed: %w\", err)\n149:return fmt.Errorf(\"unknown type: %s\", t)\n151:// CORRECT — no cause to wrap\n152:return errors.Errorf(ctx, \"unknown type: %s\", t)\n181:**fmt.Errorf**\n183:return fmt.Errorf(\"failed: %w\", err) // No context data, no stack trace\n245:**Applies when**: any `*.go` file outside `main.go`, `*_test.go`, `vendor/` calls `fmt.Errorf(...)`.\n247:**Why**: `fmt.Errorf` loses ctx-derived structured data and stack traces. Use `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"...\")` (wrapping) or `errors.Errorf(ctx, \"...\", args...)` (new error) from `github.com/bborbe/errors` instead.\n252:return fmt.Errorf(\"fetch failed: %w\", err)\n303:    return errors.Errorf(ctx, \"invalid: %s\", input)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92879bdf48abd110","session_id":"649c3b71-f1fd-46a9-a844-34ab62b5da5e","uuid":"1b7bc356-c686-4bb9-950a-4a30731e71d6","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:54:04.423Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1 (model)"}
