{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fc6ec2eb2160bd9","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:18:### RULE go-testing/no-stdlib-table-tests (MUST)\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:21:**Applies when**: a Go test file uses `t.Run` inside a `for ... range` loop instead of `DescribeTable`/`Entry`. The rule fires regardless of whether a Ginkgo suite exists in the package — stdlib table-driven tests are discouraged universally; suite-coexistence amplifies the cost.\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:22:**Enforcement**: `rules/go/no-stdlib-table-tests.yml`\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:23:**Why**: Mixed Ginkgo + stdlib tables produce inconsistent reporter output, fragmented runs, and surprises with `--focus` / `--label-filter`. Single-framework enforcement keeps test runs predictable.\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:28:// stdlib table-driven test in a Ginkgo-suite package\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:40:// Ginkgo DescribeTable\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:41:var _ = DescribeTable(\"foo\",\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:54:**Enforcement**: `rules/go/no-testing-t-direct.yml` flags every `func TestXxx(t *testing.T)` declaration. The agent decides per-finding whether the function is the legitimate Ginkgo suite entry-point (`RegisterFailHandler(Fail); RunSpecs(t, \"Suite\")`) or a stdlib-style test that needs to be ported to Ginkgo — that distinction needs reading the function body's intent, which ast-grep can't do reliably.\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:55:**Why**: Direct `testing.T` use bypasses the Ginkgo lifecycle (`BeforeEach`/`AfterEach`/`JustBeforeEach`), produces flaky setup ordering, and breaks `--focus` filtering. Use `Describe`/`Context`/`It`/`DescribeTable`/`Entry` so the suite runs as one coherent test plan.\n/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md:450:\tDescribeTable(\"unit conversions\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92879bdf48abd110","session_id":"649c3b71-f1fd-46a9-a844-34ab62b5da5e","uuid":"230690c9-18ae-424b-bd54-1c048e4d2663","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:54:23.329Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1 (model)"}
