prompt 1, which I verified defines the exact signature `(ctx, jobNamespace, executorNamespace string) (string, error)` and the exact substring `may not equal the executor namespace`) |\n| `pkg/agent_configuration.go` — `AgentConfiguration.JobNamespace` | NOT present yet — correctly framed as from prompt 1 (prompt 1 adds it + the `convert`/`TaggedConfigurations` copies) |\n| `pkg/k8s_connector.go` — `jobNamespace` schema property | NOT present yet — correctly framed as from prompt 1 |\n| `pkg/job_watcher.go` — `k8sinformers.WithNamespace(string(w.namespace))` | Verified (line 74) |\n| `pkg/factory/factory.go` — `NewJobSpawner` wiring (line 113) | Verified |\n| `CHANGELOG.md` — `## Unreleased` exists at top | Verified |\n| Handler claim (req 2: \"task stays untouched\") — `pkg/handler/task_event_handler.go:505` | Verified: on `SpawnJob` error the handler returns before `taskStore.Store`, `PublishSpawnNotification`, and any marking |\n| External symbols: `k8s.Namespace` (`type Namespace string`), `ObjectMetaBuilder.SetNamespace(k8s.Namespace)`, `Action.Matches(verb, resource)`, `CreateAction.GetNamespace()`, `fake.Clientset.PrependReactor`, `libtime.NewCurrentDateTime`/`SetNow`/`libtimetest.ParseDateTime`, `agentv1` alias (used in `config_resolver.go` + `job_spawner_test.go`) | All verified against module cache (bborbe/k8s v1.14.16, client-go v0.36.4, in-repo precedent) |\n| New test file's stdlib/internal-package approach | Valid — `package spawner` + `package spawner_test` coexist; precedent `pkg/job_watcher_internal_test.go` exists |\n| New `SpawnJob` refuse-branch Go correctness (`targetNamespace, err :=` then later `envBuilder, err :=` reuses `err`; later `_, err = ...Create`) | Verified — compiles correctly |\n| Requirement 7 exclude-list (`unexpected K8s error` namespace-independent reactor, `VolumeClaim/VolumeMountPath` pre-create error, `applyTaskIDLabel` capture reactor, IsJobActive/CountActiveJobs fixtures) | Verified against test file — all accurate |\n\n##