prompt 2 req 5). The residual-risk case (third unprotected namespace) is explicitly accepted by the spec, not a code requirement.\n- [x] External calls have timeout/cancellation — N/A (no exec/HTTP/Docker in requirements).\n- [x] New strings flowing through boundary validators have contract tests — see Boundary Coverage below.\n- [x] No `go mod vendor` anywhere in the prompt (verified by grep; `make precommit`'s `ensure` target wipes `vendor/`, so this is correctly absent).\n- [x] No cross-repo writes (no `git clone`/`git push`/`gh pr create`; verified by grep).\n- [x] Container-autonomous — no kubectl/deploy/observe steps, no operator-vs-agent split; every requirement is a file edit or a test the container can run.\n- [x] Sibling entry points covered. `ConfigSpec.Equal` is delegated to by `Config.Equal` (types.go:134/136), so the new field propagates to both entry points automatically. `configResolver.Resolve` has two lookup paths (composed + plain assignee) but both funnel through the single `convert` (config_resolver.go:73/92), so req 7 covers both. Spawner entry points are explicitly out of scope and owned by sibling prompt 2.\n\n## Documentation Placement\n- [x] No inlined reusable coding patterns (>10 lines). The inlined Go is the actual new implementation (the `ResolveJobNamespace` function, the table test, the schema test) — this is precise implementation spec, not a reusable pattern like CQRS/factory wiring.\n- [x] Coding plugin docs referenced in `<context>` (go-patterns, go-error-wrapping-guide, go-testing-guide, go-kubernetes-crd-controller-guide — all four verified present and relevant).\n- [x] Domain knowledge that outlives the prompt lives in the spec, not inlined.\n- [~] `docs/agent-crd-specification.md` (project CRD doc) is not referenced in `<context>` — acceptable, since the doc row is owned by sibling prompt 3, but a one-line cross-reference would be harmless.\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------