ction\"\n\n## Strengths\n\n- **Line-number precision is verified exact.** The `~line 225` / `~line 252` hints for `types_test.go` match the actual `priorityClassName` Describe blocks exactly; the `validateTaskTypesList` \"last helper\" claim matches the file's actual ordering.\n- **The schema-registration steps (reqs 8-9) are the right kind of defense.** Requirement 8 correctly cites the v0.5.0 `maxConcurrentJobs` prune incident from the authoritative doc comment, and requirement 9 builds a genuine level-1 contract test against the exact regression — not a shape test.\n- **Boundary-contract coverage is comprehensive** across serialization, registry, and propagation seams (reqs 4, 5, 9, 10, 11).\n- **Requirement 12's negative constraints** pre-empt the two most likely executor mistakes (running the k8s codegen unnecessarily; wiring the guard into `Validate` where the executor namespace is unknown).\n- **The verification block is a model of container autonomy** — all commands are container-executable, and it explicitly forbids the operator-only command families, correctly noting the daemon does not check their exit codes.\n- **Crisp scope boundaries across the 3-prompt set** (model / spawner / doc) match the spec's Suggested Decomposition table exactly, with the constraints section spelling out what this prompt must NOT touch.\n- Every external symbol (`errors.Errorf`) was verified against both the module source and the coding guide.\n\n## Summary\n\nA polished, fully-verified prompt: every code reference checks out against the repo, failure-mode and security coverage is complete across the sibling set, boundary-contract tests are present at every seam, and the verification is fully container-executable. The only findings are minor recommendations (a spec-mandated-but-undocumented stdlib-test deviation that is not CI-enforced, one imprecise fixture description, and one objective-wording nit). No critical issues; approve as-is or after the optional Recommendation 1 not